 ],
 "text": "Your AI assistant just spent $4,000 from your debit card on something you never asked for. It's 9am. What do you do first? Here's what the rules actually say. In the US, if you report an unauthorized debit card charge within two business days, your loss is capped at $50. Wait longer and it can rise to $500. Wait more than 60 days after your statement and you could lose all of it. So you get one move. Option A, call your bank right now and report it. Option B, ask the store for a refund first and only call the bank if they say no. Comment A or B. Part 2 shows what happens next."
